				'Bio', T(890000000005183, "At first light Daniel Kiprop still presses two fingers to the ground, even when the only tracks belong to bicycles. A Kenyan ranger taught him to read the flicker of grass before other men heard a branch move. Bulky burdens tire Daniel, so he chooses cleaner routes through rough country. Fine rifles passed him by, but an early glimpse and a well-chosen position have often served him better.") --[[ModItemUnitDataCompositeDef JAZZ_AME_09 Bio]],
