				'Bio', T(890000000005493, "A faded wool cap becomes Abraham Tekle's tiny pillow every night, a comfort kept from colder bivouacs. It followed an Ethiopian mountain campaign that ended with more men walking home than marching. Defeat made Abraham quieter rather than bitter, and he waits for a clear sight instead of demanding one. He looks worn, but hardship has left both frame and attention surprisingly difficult to shake.") --[[ModItemUnitDataCompositeDef JAZZ_AME_40 Bio]],
